## 1. Independent mechanical pass — the repo's own parser

Harness: `/Users/damian/.local-operator/sessions/675090271c24/scratchpad/audit/vi-mech.mts`
(imports `parseMessage` from the worktree's `src/i18n/messages.ts`; reads the
brief, the draft and the English catalogues; writes nothing).

$ cd $SCRATCH/audit && <worktree>/node_modules/.bin/tsx vi-mech.mts

First run exited 1 with 207 failures — **all of them from my own Latin-residue
heuristic**, which split Vietnamese words at their diacritics ("không" -> "kh",
"ng") and flagged the fragments. That was a defect in my test, not in the draft;
the check was rewritten to flag only pure-ASCII tokens that are also words of the
English source. The control run above is preserved here because a passing
harness that never failed is worth less than one whose failure was diagnosed.

Second run (before the rewrite):

FAIL mobile.computers.wait.listing: possible Latin residue "danh" ...
FAIL mobile.computers.wait.tunnel_status: possible Latin residue "status" ...
MECHANICAL: 23 FAILURE(S)   EXIT=1

Third run, after tokenising on Unicode word boundaries with the English word
list as the discriminator:

$ <worktree>/node_modules/.bin/tsx vi-mech.mts
keys: brief=44 draft=44 en=107
placeholders seen: status, name, reach
plurals in this slice: 0

MECHANICAL: PASS (0 failures)
EXIT=0

What that PASS asserts, per value: parses under `parseMessage`; parameter names
AND kinds identical to English; ICU structure identical; raw placeholder tokens
byte-identical and in order; key set and order identical to the brief; valid
JSON; NFC; no ASCII "..."; no space before punctuation; no doubled spaces;
full-stop parity; ellipsis parity; no English source word carried into a value.

Independent cross-check in Python (unicodedata + ASCII-word scan):

NFC all: True | NFD any: True       (precomposed Vietnamese, as the guide requires)
pure-ASCII words that are also English source words:
  {'Local': ['not_harness'], 'Radient': [6 keys], 'status': [3 a11y keys],
   'URL': ['radient_body'], 'name': [3 a11y keys], 'reach': [3 a11y keys]}
all other pure-ASCII words are Vietnamese syllables without diacritics
  (Thanh, Thao, bao, cao, cho, danh, do, khai, ngay, qua, quay, sang, thay, thu, truy, xa)

Byte-identical-to-English values: exactly one, `mobile.computers.row.a11y`.

